# adbreak-manager (Ad Break & Campaign Booking Manager)

## Stack
- Backend: Python 3.12, FastAPI + Pydantic v2, SQLAlchemy 2.0 + Alembic, PostgreSQL (row-level locking for BR-10), JWT (python-jose or PyJWT) with role dependencies, pytest + httpx, uv or pip + ruff
- Frontend: React 18 + Vite + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, TanStack Query, React Router, Recharts, React Hook Form + Zod, Vitest + React Testing Library
- Frontend uses only endpoints in the backend OpenAPI schema
- Local setup: Docker Compose (Postgres + API)

## Architecture
routers -> services -> models; business rules only in services/

## Behaviour
1. Never assume. If anything is unclear or missing, STOP and ask me numbered questions; log unanswered ones in docs/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md.
2. BR-01..BR-10 in docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md are the source of truth; cite rule IDs in code comments and tests.
3. Be token-efficient: no long explanations, never re-print unchanged files, show only changed code.
4. One module at a time; wait for my approval before the next.
5. Type hints everywhere, small functions, no unused code.
6. Do not run git commands; I commit myself. Do not install packages or change config outside the task without asking.
7. Do not add fields, endpoints or features not in the context without asking.
